      "side": 1,
      "message": "For this example, the only notable `HAS_TASK_*` defines which were missing was `HAS_TASK_RWSIG` and `HAS_TASK_FPSENSOR`.\n\nRight, this didn\u0027t change the behavior of any existing boards, which means we weren\u0027t relying on it (maybe because it didn\u0027t work). I think we would typically condition configs based on `SECTION_IS_RW` or `SECTION_IS_RO`, instead of `HAS_TASK_RWSIG`.\n\n---\n\nYeah, the `HAS_TASK_*_RW/RO` were foreign to me, too. These seem to show up in the opposite image. So, in the `RO` image, which doesn\u0027t contain any fpsensor code, you see `HAS_TASK_FPSENSOR_RW`. I guess these must have been some application where one image needed to know about the other image\u0027s features?\n\n---\n\nHonestly, this is a very minor fix for correctness.",
